Z||000009||Mr.Frosty||06-01-2001||11:14 AM||||You have to do a lot to Turbocharge a non-turbo Mr2,and to get to that horsepower like he was talking....It wouldn't be that high.A factory turbo Mr2 can reach those levels,but with extensive tuning and Twin turbos to boot.The factory Turbo motor is built internally stronger than the non-turbo.The stock motor won't take many runs to the redline.If it's done conservatively it might approach the power output of the factory turbo.<P>------------------<BR>85 GT Turbo intercooled||||reg||1
